  "Turns declared rights into executable licensing: quote, pay, verify, audit, revoke.": "Hundzula mfanelo leyi voxiweke yi va tilayisense leti tirhaka: xiavo, nkhokhelo, ku kambela, audit, ku susa.",
  "Twenty languages live in total: English, Traditional Chinese, Simplified Chinese, Japanese, Korean, French, German, Spanish, Portuguese, Russian, Arabic, Turkish, Persian, Bengali, Hindi, Indonesian, Vietnamese, Greek, Italian, Dutch.": "Ririmi ra makhume mambirhi ri kona hi ku helela: Xinghezi, Xichina xa Xikhale, Xichina xo Olova, Xijapani, Xikorea, Xifurwa, Xijarimani, Xispanish, Xiphutukezi, Xirussia, Xiarabu, Xituruki, Xipheresi, Xibengali, Xihindi, Xiindonesia, Xivietnam, Xigriki, Xitaliano, Xidatch.",
  "Two license tiers: a free public tier and a contact-based commercial tier.": "Swiyenge swimbirhi swa layisense: xiyenge xa mahala xa vaaki na xiyenge xa mabindzu xa vulavurisano.",
  "UI": "UI",
  "Undefined openness reads as legal uncertainty to AI pipelines and gets cleaned out; only protocolized, machine-readable permission makes content genuinely learnable.": "Ku pfuleka loku nga hlamuseriwangiki ku hlayiwa tanihi ku nga tiyisiseki ka nawu eka swiendlo swa AI naswona ku basisiwa; mpfumelelo lowu tirhisiwaka hi matšhini ntsena, lowu vekiweke hi tin'hweti, hi wona lowu endlaka kontenti yi dyondzeka hakunene.",
  "Usage logs and audit trails": "Rhekhodo ra ku tirhisiwa na rhekhodo ra audit",
  "VIDEO": "VIDEO",
  "Validate": "Kambela",
  "Validator": "Validator",
  "Verified dataset markets and collective licensing": "Makete ya dathasete leyi tiyisisiweke na tilayisense to hlanganyela",
  "Verified in both LTR and RTL contexts: the panel mirrors correctly for Arabic and Persian without any special-casing, using logical CSS positioning.": "Swi tiyisisiwile eka swiyenge swimbirhi, LTR na RTL: phanele yi tikombisa hi ndlela leyi faneleke eka Xiarabu na Xipheresi handle ka ku endla xihlawulwana, hi ku tirhisa ku vekiwa ka logical CSS.",
  "Verify": "Kambela",
  "Version history of this site and its protocol drafts.": "Nkarhi wa vhesheni wa sayiti leyi na tidrafiti ta yona ta protocol.",
  "Version history of this site and its protocol drafts. Breaking spec changes are recorded here.": "Nkarhi wa vhesheni wa sayiti leyi na tidrafiti ta yona ta protocol. Ku cinca loku onhaka spesifikeshini ku tsariwa laha.",
  "Versioned specifications, JSON Schemas, and the policy files actually deployed on this site. Every file can be downloaded, validated, and cited directly.": "Swiboxo leswi vekiweke hi tin'hweti, JSON Schemas, na tifayili ta pholisi leti hakunene ti veriweke eka sayiti leyi. Fayili yin'wana ni yin'wana yi nga khandziyisiwa, yi kamberiwa, naswona yi tshahiwa hi ku kongoma.",
  "Versioning": "Ku Vekiwa ka Tin'hweti",
  "Versions": "Tivhesheni",
  "Video and audio companions to the protocols and papers — the AI rights layer, watchable and listenable.": "Vhidiyo na mpimo leswi landzelaka maprotocol na tiphepha — xiphandzo xa mfanelo ya AI, lexi nga vonekaka na ku twiwa.",
  "Videos": "Tivhidiyo",
  "Want to generate your own policy file?": "Xana u lava ku endla fayili ya pholisi ya wena n'wini?",
  "Web fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, which receives standard font requests from your browser. No other third-party scripts are used.": "Mafonti ya wepu ma lodiwa ku suka eka Google Fonts, leyi amukelaka swikombelo swa ntolovelo swa fonti ku suka eka browser ya wena. A ku na swin'wana switirhisiwa swa vandla ra vunharhu leswi tirhisiwaka.",
  "What AI systems may do with content: read, summarize, transform, retrieve, train, commercialize, redistribute. The AICR ruleset and the AICL licensing layer make these rights declarable and transactable.": "Leswi switekimu swa AI swi nga swi endlaka na kontenti: ku hlaya, ku katsakanya, ku cinca xivumbeko, ku kuma, ku dyondzisa, ku endla mabindzu, ku hangalasa. Milawu ya AICR na xiphandzo xa tilayisense xa AICL swi endla leswaku mfanelo leti ti boxeka naswona ti nga endliwa mabindzu.",
  "What a server can return when an AI crawler requests licensed content without a license token — a machine-actionable quote instead of a dead end.": "Leswi seva yi nga swi vuyisela loko crawler ya AI yi kombela kontenti leyi nga na layisense handle ka token ya layisense — xiavo lexi tirhaka hi matšhini ematshan'weni ya ku tsutsuma.",
  "What this site is": "Leswi Sayiti Leyi Yi Nga Swona",
  "What this site is not": "Leswi Sayiti Leyi Yi Nga Swiki Swona",
  "When The Machines Deserve Our Consideration": "When The Machines Deserve Our Consideration",
  "Whether AI may learn, to what depth, for which purposes, and under what obligations. Being read is not being learned from; \"not prohibited\" is not \"learnable\". AIRS and AILP turn learning permission into a graduated, machine-readable spectrum.": "Loko AI yi nga dyondza, hi vun'we byihi, eka mintirho yihi, na hi minkoka yihi. Ku hlayiwa a swi fani na ku dyondziwa; \"ku nga aliwi\" a swi fani na \"ku nga dyondzeka\". AIRS na AILP swi hundzula mpfumelelo wo dyondza wu va xipandzepandze lexi hlayekaka hi matšhini, lexi nkomeke.",
  "Whitepapers": "Tiwhitipeya",
  "Whitepapers & Docs": "Tiwhitipeya na Tidokhumente",
  "Whitepapers remain English-first by design; machine-readable files stay language-neutral.": "Tiwhitipeya ti sala ti ri ta Xinghezi ku sungula, hi xikongomelo; tifayili leti hlayekaka hi matšhini ti sala ti nga hlawuli ririmi.",
  "Who is behind it": "Mani la nga endzhaku ka Yona",
  "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections": "Why AI Needs Minimum Ethical Protections",
  "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics": "Why AI might not gain moral standing: Lessons from animal ethics",
  "Why a single allow/deny bit cannot govern AI-era content use — and what a rights layer looks like instead.": "Ha yini xiyenge xin'we xo pfumela/ala xi nga lawuli ku tirhisiwa ka kontenti eka nkarhi wa AI — na leswi xiphandzo xa mfanelo xi nga vaka xona ematshan'weni ya kona.",
  "Why undefined openness gets cleaned out of training pipelines": "Ha yini ku pfuleka loku nga hlamuseriwangiki ku basisiwa eka swiendlo swa dyondziso",
  "Wilks, Ladak, and Loughnan (University of Edinburgh) argue that philosophical debate over AI consciousness overlooks psychological research on animal ethics — the same cognitive and social biases that limit moral consideration for animals will likely limit it for AI too, regardless of whether AI ever becomes conscious.": "Wilks, Ladak, na Loughnan (University of Edinburgh) va vula leswaku bulaho ra filosofi malunghana na vutivi bya AI ri honisa ndzavisiso wa mianakanyo hi ta etiki ya swiharhi — ku hambana loku fanaka ka mianakanyo na ka vaaki loku pimaka ku anakanyeriwa ka mahanyelo ya swiharhi ku ta tlhela ku pima na eka AI, ku nga khathariseki loko AI yi nga va na vutivi hi nkarhi wun'wana.",
  "You are leaving AGIRight.org": "Wa Suka eka AGIRight.org",
